alities in provided labs"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia (Ca2+ 12.5 mg/dL)", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase (150 U/L)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Neoplastic Process with Hypercalcemia and Elevated ALP", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.31529164477141347, "posterior": 0.12831701955217167, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Unintentional weight loss is a nonspecific but meaningful sign of malignancy, providing moderate support for B1 and weak support for B4.2."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of bone pain and monoclonal proteins weakens the neoplastic hypothesis, but recent weight loss and elevated ALP maintain some suspicion."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["multiple myeloma", "lymphoma", "carcinoma with bony metastases"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Medication-Induced Hypercalcemia", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.048, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of thiazide/vitamin D toxicity evidence does not confirm medication-induced causes, but antacid use remains a potential contributor."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Metabolic Bone Disease with Hypercalcemia", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.104, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Classic signs of hyperparathyroidism are absent, but low urine sodium and elevated ALP could still suggest chronic bone disease variants."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Hepatobiliary Disorder with Cholestatic Pattern", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2695743562795586, "posterior": 0.18456640588724602, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Isolated ALP elevation without jaundice provides limited support for hepatobiliary disease, which typically presents with more pronounced cholestatic features."], "evidence_against": ["Normal urine and lack of inflammation markers reduce likelihood of infectious/inflammatory hepatobiliary disease, but isolated ALP elevation remains ambiguous."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B4.1", "B4.2", "B4.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": ["Primary biliary cholangitis", "Extrahepatic cholestasis", "Hepatitis with biliary injury"]}, "B4.1": {"id": "B4.1", "label": "Primary Biliary Cholangitis (Autoimmune Cholestatic Liver Disease)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.104, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Negative ANA and lack of jaundice provide weak evidence against B4.1, but insufficient to exclude it given its low specificity."]}, "B4.2": {"id": "B4.2", "label": "Extrahepatic Biliary Obstruction with Cholestatic Pattern", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.063, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of obstructive symptoms weakly argues against B4.2 as the primary explanation for ALP elevation."]}, "B4.3": {"id": "B4.3", "label": "Hepatitis with Biliary Injury (Viral/Toxic/Autoimmune)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.018, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "B4", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal transaminases and lack of viral markers weakly disfavor B4.3 as the cause of ALP elevation."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia and Elevated ALP", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.033, "danger": 0.